7592186277933 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186275688 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186277933 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186275822 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186277933 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186276046 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186277933 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186277194 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186277933 #edb/ref 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186277933 #edb/ref 1077 "selection" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186277933 #edb/ref 1078 #edb/ref 17592186275822 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186277933 #edb/ref 1079 #uuid "7500f3f7-1bc0-59bc-acac-f110b13ae378" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186278099 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186275845 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186278099 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186276647 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186278099 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186277066 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186278099 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186277347 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186278099 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186277498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186278099 #edb/ref 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186278099 #edb/ref 1077 "selection" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186278099 #edb/ref 1078 #edb/ref 17592186277066 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186278099 #edb/ref 1079 #uuid "d5b5dc04-4d52-5d46-b88e-b20b9902f553" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186278284 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186278099 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186278284 #edb/ref 1069 "q-160369" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186278284 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186278284 #edb/ref 1071 "A triangle $S$ has vertices at $(-2,5),(4,-3),(3,2).$ Which of the following are coordinates of the vertices of ${S}^{′},$ the image of $S$ under the counterclockwise rotation ${R}_{{180}^{∘}}$ by an angle of ${180}^{∘}$ about the origin?\n\n- $(2,5)$\n- $(-4,-3)$\n- $(-3,-2)$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186278284 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "4fb94a38-de9a-5a83-b5a3-84ca0f8fdab4" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186278284 #edb/ref 1074 "The counterclockwise rotation ${R}_{{180}^{∘}}$ by an angle of ${180}^{∘}$ is given by the matrix\n\n$$\nR=[\\begin{aligned}-1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & -1\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nTo find the image of $S$ under the action of ${R}_{{180}^{∘}},$ we first create a matrix $X$ containing all of the vertices of $S:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}X & =[\\begin{aligned}-2 & 4 & 3 \\\\ 5 & -3 & 2\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we compute the image of $X$ under ${R}_{{180}^{∘}}$ by calculating the matrix product $RX:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}RX & =[\\begin{aligned}-1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & -1\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}-2 & 4 & 3 \\\\ 5 & -3 & 2\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}2 & -4 & -3 \\\\ -5 & 3 & -2\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the coordinates of the respective vertices of ${S}^{′}$ are $(2,-5),(-4,3),(-3,-2).$\n\nSo, the correct answer is \"III only.\"" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186278325 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186277933 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186278325 #edb/ref 1069 "q-160624" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186278325 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186278325 #edb/ref 1071 "![](images/c3/c32886c161e347daa9bf6fa7215f8a09abc4334632c33020c31ade6dfc4e7315.png)\n\nConsider the vector $v$ shown above. Find the vector $Av$ given that \n\n$$\nA=[\\begin{aligned}-1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & -1\\end{aligned}].\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186278325 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "ff455380-864a-530d-ba7f-afe2837adda6" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186278325 #edb/ref 1074 "Consider the standard basis ${i,j}$ of the Euclidean plane ${R}^{2}$ and the unit square spanned by the vectors. Computing the images of ${i,j}$ under $A$, we get the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{i}^{′} & =A(i)=[\\begin{aligned}-1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & -1\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}-1 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]=-i \\\\ {j}^{′} & =A(j)=[\\begin{aligned}-1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & -1\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ -1\\end{aligned}]=-j\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nAs a result, we obtain the following diagram:\n\n![](images/9f/9fae3ec0ada3008937d88e4e76374a56da4369b1821cfee072c90d88b562df46.png)\n\nSo, the matrix represents a rotation of $\\pi $ radians (counterclockwise or clockwise) about the origin.\n\nTherefore, in order to find $Av$, we need to rotate $v$ (counterclockwise or clockwise) by an angle of $\\pi $ radians, as shown below.\n\n![](images/ed/ed1a5e8a05ee0d9994d8ba90c02463fbf96525b1cd851bec685a005a34834f81.png)" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186278330 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186277885 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186278330 #edb/ref 1069 "q-160644" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186278330 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186278330 #edb/ref 1071 "A triangle $S$ has vertices at $(2,-3),(3,1),(-4,-1).$ Which of the following are coordinates of the vertices of ${S}^{′},$ the image of $S$ under the counterclockwise rotation ${R}_{{270}^{∘}}$ by an angle of ${270}^{∘}$ about the origin?\n\n- $(3,2)$\n- $(1,-3)$\n- $(-1,4)$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186278330 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "932ec8a6-f54a-5a6e-82db-611776aadb8f" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186278330 #edb/ref 1074 "The counterclockwise rotation ${R}_{{270}^{∘}}$ by an angle of ${270}^{∘}$ is given by the matrix\n\n$$\nR=[\\begin{aligned}0 & 1 \\\\ -1 & 0\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nTo find the image of $S$ under the action of ${R}_{{270}^{∘}},$ we first create a matrix $X$ containing all of the vertices of $S:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}X & =[\\begin{aligned}2 & 3 & -4 \\\\ -3 & 1 & -1\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we compute the image of $X$ under ${R}_{{270}^{∘}}$ by calculating the matrix product $RX:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}RX & =[\\begin{aligned}0 & 1 \\\\ -1 & 0\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}2 & 3 & -4 \\\\ -3 & 1 & -1\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}-3 & 1 & -1 \\\\ -2 & -3 & 4\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the coordinates of the respective vertices of ${S}^{′}$ are $(-3,-2),(1,-3),(-1,4).$\n\nSo, the correct answer is \"II and III only.\"" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186348645 #edb/ref 1080 "I only" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186348645 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045499 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186348645 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "17672d7b-1484-5a23-8f4a-1d0c8fe3f938" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186348955 #edb/ref 1080 "II only" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186348955 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045499 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186348955 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "382f3226-220a-530e-82f8-7d3559509fc1" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186349181 #edb/ref 1080 "I, II, and III" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186349181 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045499 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186349181 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "50edb2a8-35bd-5f50-ae59-221642a50ecd" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186349304 #edb/ref 1080 "images/97/979157d993a86617fabf4b2dfacc6d4c1d973885b42be081b4bcffb36058e091.png" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186349304 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045497 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186349304 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "5d52e72e-e45b-521b-8ee0-c71997fb8ca9" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186349321 #edb/ref 1080 "images/f4/f4d4d52cb24bd1e3dd4bc37736533693ff89e6b08f495f8541f23abde995a5b9.png" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186349321 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045497 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186349321 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "5f423739-805a-5241-83e8-6c43a2d06485" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186349549 #edb/ref 1080 "images/cf/cf449d44237c85963bf4fbb134da290b39aac4ebd0b128313052cbd1970db67f.png" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186349549 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045497 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186349549 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "7765856b-43ca-5356-bbc9-33e765c33ae1" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186349785 #edb/ref 1080 "images/4b/4bf42e3bdeb61feccd68cf4eeb9e3c4a40e8b903a5739df77c993e9aa4abc993.png" #edb/ref